      "diagnosticStartSeconds": null,
      "startSeconds": 1423.3,
      "endSeconds": 1435.78,
      "audiblePhrase": "The problem starts with the nature of renewables themselves. Sources such as solar panels and wind farms are intermittent, which means they only generate electricity when the sun is shining or the wind is blowing, and not at other times."
    },
    {
      "question": 32,
      "responseKey": "l4-form__32",
